    "reading": "Density 0.851 (sub-rules present): -0.004 and -0.046, both CIs including zero. Density 1.369 (no sub-rules): +0.071, CI including zero. Density 2.031 (sub-rules present): -0.154, -0.171, -0.104, -0.238, every CI excluding zero. Density 4.126 (no sub-rules): -0.113, CI excluding zero. Sub-rules are present in the runs at 0.851 and 2.031 and absent in those at 1.369 and 4.126, so they are on both sides of the split and cannot explain it; reasoning density is monotone with the outcome and puts the threshold between 1.37 and 2.03. This REFINES PR #289, which concluded from the 4.126 run that the rationale is 'necessary and sufficient': it is enough rationale that is sufficient, and one corpus with no sub-rules and below-explanatory density produces no interaction at all."
